# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/
# ...and node_modules itself when it is a SYMLINK. A trailing-slash pattern
# matches only a directory, so a `node_modules -> ...` symlink (which is how
# worktrees here borrow the main checkout's install) sails past `node_modules/`
# and gets picked up by `git add -A`. Committing one breaks every OTHER machine
# that checks the branch out: the link resolves to a path that exists on one box
# only, and the build fails on a missing react-native rather than on anything to
# do with the change.
node_modules

